  reason: "The one producer arm for std.compiler_entry NativeIngressDriver services (gunbc.target_binding NativeServeProgramProducer { entry, probe }), the instrument the operator ruling of 2026-10-03 asked for beside the arm. Its host part is only what no .dag fold can do: emit and build through the existing prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry, spawn the built service with an argv the reader renders (gunbc.native_serve_probe_plan native_serve_probe_launch, over the one renderer of a binding's arguments, gunbc.http_ingress http_ingress_binding_arguments), read the address it announces, write the requests the reader names to real TCP connections, and carry the bytes that came back out unjudged; run each of the reader's refused launches and carry its status and stderr; and for the deadline phase start each of the reader's deadline launches on its own, send it its one request (which may name the port of a loopback listener the host holds and never answers, the low-CPU stall), and await that exact process's exit, carrying announcement, response and status; and for the unix-socket phase (gunbc.plans.converged_ingress M2b) choose the socket's path in a fresh owner-only directory, ask the reader for the subject's argv over that path (native_serve_probe_unix_launch_argv), exchange every request over that socket (native_serve_unix_exchange, through the one exchange body native_serve_exchange_on), and report the account the host's own effective uid resolves to (native_serve_host_account), which the reader compares with the peer the service's kernel attested; before the subject starts it leaves a stale socket at the subject's path, and it launches the binary once on a second path it listens on itself, carrying that launch's status and stderr and whether a connection by that path still reached its listener. Every verdict -- the cases, what each owes, the join of responses to cases, the refused starts, the deadline exits -- is native_serve_probe_standing, evaluated by the host and mapped through cli_run classify_exit, so the host adds none. It is ONE arm generic over its entry AND over the row's probe (gunbc.native_serve_probe_plan NativeServeProbe): the reader module and the declared phase set (peer instance, refused launch, deadline exit, unix socket) are fields of the binding row, read by read_native_serve_binding through gunbc.instrument_targets and handed to the run as NativeServePhases with the launches as NativeServeLaunches, so the host branches on no binding and spells no flag; a row declaring a phase its reader cannot judge, or a reader judging a phase the row does not declare, is refused before anything is built (gunbc.native_serve_probe_plan native_serve_phase_refusals). THE PURPOSE TEST (DESIGN section 3, v1 maintenance standing): this growth serves the v2 self-host program, because the services it makes runnable are emitted .dag folds -- the device-crypto verifier (extdeps.crypto.signature verify_signature, extdeps.apple.app_attest verify_attestation and verify_assertion) that the native broker will link in process -- and it adds no v1 semantics. It also starts a SECOND instance of the same entry as the local server its bound REST handler is pointed at (native broker 2N), reads that instance's announced port, and asks native_serve_probe_requests for the requests with that port as the argument, so the request bytes are still the reader's. The emitter's side of the native realization (the program descriptor's resolution and the rendered main) is rostered separately, in gunbc.native_ingress_emission_seed_growth.",

  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,

  trigger: "Delete these declarations when gunbc test's producer dispatch is emitted rather than hand-mirrored (the capability gunbc.target_invocation_seed_growth names for target_invocation_host as a whole) AND an emitted driver can spawn a built service, exchange bytes with it over a TCP or unix socket, hold a listener of its own (the silent TCP listener, and the live unix listener a launch must not displace), read the account its own uid resolves to, await the service's exit and hand what it observed to a .dag fold, SUFFICIENT FOR //gunbc/instruments:native-serve, //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-unix, //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-device-crypto, //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-startup-refusal, //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-startup-slow and //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-startup-overrun to run with no hand-authored producer body. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE IT: moving the spawn or the socket exchange to another host file; folding the reader into Rust.",

  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/native_lane_runner.rs run_native_serve_program, NativeServeProgramRun, NativeServePhases and NativeServeLaunches, called once from src/v1/stage0/src/target_invocation_host.rs run_native_serve_program (which reads the row through read_native_serve_binding), behind gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:native-serve, //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-unix and //gunbc/instruments:native-serve-device-crypto"
